<!-- Main Content -->
<div class="main-text" style="text-align: justify;">
    <p><b><i><h1>About AgriLearnPal</h1></b><br>
        <strong>AgriLearnPal</strong> is an honours project developed as part of a student’s final-year research in computing. 
        It combines <strong>machine learning</strong> and <strong>web technologies</strong> to create an interactive and educational 
        platform for crop analysis.<br><br>

        The project focuses on crops growable in the UK, such as <strong>potatoes, apples, and berries</strong>. The goal is 
        to provide an accessible tool that helps users recognize different crops, assess their health, and gain 
        insights into best cultivation practices.<br><br>

        This project was inspired by the increasing role of <strong>digital tools in education</strong>. Agriculture remains 
        a crucial yet often overlooked subject in modern learning. <strong>AgriLearnPal</strong> is designed to help students 
        and enthusiasts explore crops, analyze plant health, and gain valuable insights through an intuitive and 
        easy-to-use web application.<br><br>

        By integrating <strong>machine learning with agriculture</strong>, this project aims to bridge the gap between 
        <strong>technology and farming education</strong>, promoting sustainability and knowledge in UK agriculture.
    </i></p>
